 "notes": "Only page 0 has widgets (the landscape form); pages 1-3 are block-by-block instructions with no blanks. The 8 check-in rows map to check_ins[] columns. Column 5 'ST or TF' maps to check_ins[].strike_team_or_task_force (enum ST/TF, written as-is). Pathless: column 16 'Data Provided to Resources Unit' (the schema does not keep it), and Signature_18 (signature). Check-In Location checkboxes are a multi-select ('complete all that apply'): contains. Departure Point, Date and Time is one cell per row, stored as one string. Coverage is 148/157 = 94.3% mapped, above the ~90% target: the form is almost entirely the check-in table and every remaining column is something a Resources Unit keeps."
